    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d933">

                <pb facs="0859" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39)/369: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hamburg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Keblinger</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-27T15:00:00+01:00">December 27,
                            1939—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. All vessels detained by prize control authorities en route to the United
                    States have now been released with the exception of steamships <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Korsnaes</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Everoja</hi>,
                    committed to Prize Court proceedings, and Estonian steamships <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hildur</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Osmussar</hi>
                    and the Norwegian <hi rendition="#italic">Novasli</hi> which are still being
                    investigated. American bound consignments on Finnish steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dione</hi> and Estonian <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vaindlo</hi> (see Department’s telegram 207, and my telegram No. 241<anchor
                        n="18" xml:id="d933-f1"/>) are also still being investigated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Keblinger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
